{
  "_doc": "Room + sensor registry of the 3D hospital (hospital-3d/). Owner: Member 1. Single source of truth for room_id <-> sensor_id. Read by hospital-3d (3D placement, sliders) and by backend/sensor_ingestion (python -m sensor_ingestion.registry registers missing rooms/sensors in PostgreSQL). Every sensor and room of sample-sensors.json / sample-building.json is included unchanged; corridors, halls and stairwells are additional rooms. sensor_type uses only the agreed enum (smoke_heat, co, current). placement: ceiling → u/v = fraction of the room footprint (u west→east, v north→south); wall/panel → wall side n|e|s|w, u = fraction along that wall (west→east or north→south), h = height in metres.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "building_id": "HOSPITAL-DEMO-01",
  "floor_id": "floor_1",

  "sensor_types": {
    "smoke_heat": { "device": "Multi-criteria smoke + heat detector (ceiling)", "fields": { "smoke": "ppm", "temperature": "degC" } },
    "co":         { "device": "Carbon-monoxide detector (wall, 1.5 m)",           "fields": { "co": "ppm" } },
    "current":    { "device": "Current transformer on a sub-distribution circuit", "fields": { "current": "A" } }
  },

  "rooms": [
